    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e57f5a19_1dbeee19",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1523797
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-17T16:48:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The script does not treat a lack of `named-i2c-port`\u0027s as an error, though. It continues executing looking for other components and then returns success if no further issues are found. If this is truly an error, it should fail the build, or it will be ignored; if not a fatal error, this introduces noise to the build logs and is misleading.\n\nIs this script intended to convert a devicetree into a JSON description of key components, or is it intended to validate a devicetree? If it is the latter, I think we need a better source of truth of what is expected. For instance we have real EC boards in early bring-up that compile fine but don\u0027t have a `named-i2c-port` [yet] and we also have pure-Zephyr boards that wouldn\u0027t use it because `named-i2c-port` isn\u0027t mandatory unless you\u0027re shimming in legacy CrOS EC drivers.\n\nSomething like comitting a copy of the component manfiest for each board and alerting on changes would do a better job of catching devicetree msitakes/regressions in my opinion, if that is one of the goals here. (if a developer modifies the DT intentionally by adding/removing a device, they regenerate the component manifest, commit it, and it\u0027ll be easy to see in code review)\n\nI took the output of `zmake configure -a --clobber` and the list of Zephyr targets that shows the `No named-i2c-ports node found` error are `axii`, `bloonchipper`, `ite-aic`, `minimal-it8xx2`, `minimal-posix`, `ocelot_ite` for reference",
      "parentUuid": "9cba9af3_9fae59fb",
      "revId": "bb82050d464b9eab573cd6e04b3a3afd7080b0c5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5d4e4851_74bbc565",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000407
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-17T18:02:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should fail the build, including the lack of `named-i2c-port`. We need to reprioritize this old known task: b/310998625.\n\nThe script is for the former. It doesn\u0027t care about the correctness of the device tree but it cares the generated component manifest. We don\u0027t know any missing components in the manifest until the factory process, that is usually too late and we have to requal the a new EC image for its updated manifest. We need to have some heuristic to detect earlier.\n\nHaving a copy of the component manifest is also a good idea. We can do so for a few of already-shipped projects.\n\n`axii` is a detachable base. `bloonchipper` is a fingerprint MCU project. The other projects are for experimental. For these experiemental, we may use `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_BRINGUP` to skip them.\n\nWe can use `CONFIG_FINGERPRINT_SENSOR` and `CONFIG_DETACHABLE_BASE` as a blocklist to skip running `cme.py`. And use `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_BRINGUP` to forgive the `cme.py` failure (not fail the build but still print the error messages and a final message indicating the errors are forgiven).",
      "parentUuid": "e57f5a19_1dbeee19",
      "revId": "bb82050d464b9eab573cd6e04b3a3afd7080b0c5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b0680663_fcef42c5",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-17T18:55:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should merge this CL as is.  b/310998625 is already open to fix cme.py to generate a build failure for fatal errors.\n\nThat effort likely needs to fix the false positives and correct any boards that truly are missing `named-i2c-port`.\n\nBut right now, the \"error\" message from cme.py is just adding noise to the logs.",
      "parentUuid": "5d4e4851_74bbc565",
      "revId": "bb82050d464b9eab573cd6e04b3a3afd7080b0c5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
